# Verified experimentally: npm's packer does not apply .gitignore/.npmignore
# exclusions to anything matched by a package.json `files` entry — a bare
# directory or a glob in `files` ships its full contents regardless of any
# ignore file. The real defense against shipping skills/.venv/,
# skills/biomedparse/BiomedParse/ (a live git clone), and
# skills/biomedparse/weights/ (~1.7GB) is package.json's `files` array
# enumerating real source files individually instead of listing "skills" as
# a directory. This file is not load-bearing for packaging; it stays for
# tools that read .npmignore for other purposes, and to mirror .gitignore.
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store

skills/.venv/
skills/.uv-constraints.txt
skills/**/__pycache__/

skills/biomedparse/BiomedParse/
skills/biomedparse/weights/

tests/
